<article class="post post-with-toc">
<header class="post-header">
<h1>Why internal links matter</h1>
<p class="dek">Internal links help readers and search engines find the rest of your site. Here is how to add them without overthinking it.</p>
<div class="post-meta">
<address>
<ul class="people" role="list" aria-label="Written by">
<li class="person"><span><a rel="author" href="/blog/authors/asif/">Asif</a><span class="person-role">Founder of SerpDad</span></span></li>
</ul>
</address>
<p>Published <time datetime="2026-09-14">14 September 2026</time>. Updated <time datetime="2026-10-20">20 October 2026</time></p>
<p class="reading-time"><time datetime="PT1M">1 min read</time></p>
<p>Filed under <a href="/blog/category/on-page-seo/">On-page SEO</a></p>
</div>
</header>
<details class="toc-inline">
<summary>Contents</summary>
<nav aria-label="Contents">
<ol>
<li><a href="#readers-use-them-to-keep-going">Readers use them to keep going</a></li>
<li><a href="#search-engines-use-them-to-find-and-rank-pages">Search engines use them to find and rank pages</a></li>
